For machines behind an HTTP proxy that intercepts TLS and refuses Tailscale's protocol upgrades but allows
WebSockets (seen in another AI agent's sandbox: CONNECT works, then 403 on POST /ts2021). Tailscale 1.106+.
- Control: after the normal dial fails with "unexpected HTTP response", connect over WebSocket, as the browser
  (js/wasm) client always does. TS_CONTROL_WEBSOCKET=1 tries it first. Noise still runs inside.
- DERP: links in Tailscale's own opt-in feature/derpwebsocket, which falls back to WebSockets the same way;
  TS_DERP_WEBSOCKET=1 skips the DERP upgrade attempt and uses WebSockets from the start.
Tested 2026-11-26: signed in and reached a home computer with both control and DERP over WebSocket (forced),
64 ms ping via DERP; ~5 Mbit/s vs ~21 Mbit/s on the normal DERP upgrade through the same proxy.
Apply: cd tailscale-src && patch -p1 < tailscale-control-websocket.patch; run tailscaled with HTTPS_PROXY set.

